    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2608" root="بشر" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُبُشِّرٌ</span></b> , in the hand writing of J <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُبَشِّرٌ</span>, [and so in
my copies of the S,] a word of which there is not
the like except in the instances of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُنُوِّطٌ</span> [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُنَوِّطٌ</span>],
a certain bird, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَادِى تُهُلِّكَ</span> [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُهَلِّكَ</span>?] and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَادِى</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُضُلِّلَ</span> [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُضَلِّلَ</span>] and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَادِى تُخُيِّبَ</span> [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُخَيِّبَ</span>],
(TA,) <i>A certain bird, called the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صُفَارِيَّة</span>: (S, K:)
n. un. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>. (K.)

